+
+### Patterns discovered
+- WhatsApp Flows data-exchange uses a specific encryption protocol: RSA-OAEP to unwrap per-request AES key, AES-128-GCM for payload, IV flipped for response
+- Public endpoints (called by Meta) are mounted directly on `app` in index.ts, not under /api/rainbow admin routes
+- The existing checkin-form-flow.ts is the Baileys fallback (text-based) — WhatsApp Flows is the native Cloud API equivalent
+- Dev/test mode supports unencrypted plain JSON payloads (when no private key is configured)
